35,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The transport receipts show distance drives cost. The rate sheet confirms public beds are fixed at 1,100 yen. We need to control travel distance to stop the deficit.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The canteen closure means two hours daily lost to cooking. A place with staff solves that. But the lottery is a trap; one date shift means resubmitting nine pages.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The seniors confirm mixing only happens when we sleep together. But attendance shows a fifth never came, and most dropped out by winter.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Eight to a room, lights out at eleven. That explains the exhaustion. I need to know if the coastal option offers better rest.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The deposit is non-refundable. If someone cancels, the rest of us pay for their empty bed. That is an unacceptable financial risk.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, that non-refundable deposit is a direct threat to our account. We must avoid options with rigid headcount penalties.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, agreed. But the lottery’s rigidity is worse. If we pick a public centre, one schedule change forces a nine-page resubmission. That is pure administrative waste.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Toshio, the lottery risk is real, but the attendance data is worse. A fifth never came, and most left by winter. We need a setting that keeps them engaged, not just a booking.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, the attendance drop is concerning, but eight to a room is a physical barrier to rest. I cannot train effectively in those conditions.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, the deposit risk is real, but the train data is worse. A third cannot arrive by nine without paying for a bed. We need a location that solves both.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, the train data confirms the risk. If a third need beds, our fixed fee model collapses. We must price the actual accommodation, not just the camp.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, the cooking duty is solved by staff, but the lottery is a trap. One date shift means resubmitting nine pages. That administrative burden is unacceptable for the organizers.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Jonathan, eight to a room is unacceptable. But the seniors are right: mixing only happens when we sleep together. We need a place that allows shared space without the overcrowding.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, shared space is vital, but eight to a room is a health hazard. I need a setting that guarantees adequate rest before we discuss social dynamics.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
